  "question": {
    "text": "The vertical component of the earth&#39;s magnetic field is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> at any place where the angle of dip is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>37</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The earth&#39;s resultant magnetic field at that place will be (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mn>37</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>)"
